From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 17:08:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: Add the NMI interrupt controller

The A733 has the NMI controller of the A523 in the PRCM block, at offset
0x320 with the same control, enable and pending registers. The PMIC
interrupt of the boards reaches the SoC through its NMI pad.

Add the node. The registers sit in the PRCM at 0x07010320 (manual
section 4.2.5.28 to 4.2.5.30), the controller raises interrupt 220, GIC
SPI 188 (manual section 12.1, interrupt sources).

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards; the controller is
enabled towards the application CPUs only, not the RISC-V core, and
stays clear at rest; on one board a short of the power key test pads
raised the PMIC interrupt through it.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
index 892c50f16680..e4cc492a5565 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
@@ -1292,6 +1292,15 @@ r_ccu: clock-controller@7010000 {
 			#reset-cells = <1>;
 		};
 
+		nmi_intc: interrupt-controller@7010320 {
+			compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-nmi",
+				     "allwinner,sun55i-a523-nmi";
+			reg = <0x07010320 0xc>;
+			interrupt-controller;
+			#interrupt-cells = <2>;
+			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 188 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH 0>;
+		};
+
 		r_wdt: watchdog@7021000 {
 			compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-wdt",
 				     "allwinner,sun55i-a523-wdt";
